  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The curve contain three activated complex as shown below in the curve.In the curve P and Q are the intermediates. The step with the highest activation energy is the rate determining step. Hence, in the given reaction, two intermediates, three activated complexes are involved and step-II is the rate determining step.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0067_f1b0a3fd9ef9.png\" style=\"width: 378px; height: 196px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>"
